febris-simulation-sdk provides a prebuilt DLL with a flat C ABI and no CMake
targets. Link it the plain way:

    find_path(FEBRIS_SIM_INCLUDE_DIR FebrisSimApi.h)
    find_library(FEBRIS_SIM_LIBRARY Febris.CppSimulationLibrary)
    target_include_directories(main PRIVATE ${FEBRIS_SIM_INCLUDE_DIR})
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE ${FEBRIS_SIM_LIBRARY})

vcpkg deploys Febris.CppSimulationLibrary.dll next to your executable in the
applocal step. Alternatively skip linking entirely and bind at runtime:

    LoadLibrary("Febris.CppSimulationLibrary.dll") + GetProcAddress

Every export is declared in FebrisSimApi.h, which also documents the status
codes, the buffer convention and the enum values.
